-- Seed: Traditional Medicare (Part B) coverage, from the CMS RVU file.
--
-- Source: CMS National Physician Fee Schedule Relative Value File
-- RVU26C (July 2026 release, published 06/30/2026), file
-- PPRRVU2026_Jul_nonQPP.csv. Read DETERMINISTICALLY — the status
-- indicator and the RVUs are CSV columns, so there is no hallucination
-- surface and source_quote is the row as published.
--
-- National non-facility payment = total non-facility RVU x the 33.4009
-- conversion factor, both taken from the file. Locality payment varies
-- by GPCI, and the answer text says so rather than implying the figure
-- is what a specific practice receives.
--
-- Status codes are CMS's own, from Attachment A of RVU26C.pdf. Only
-- A/R/T RVUs are used for Medicare payment. CMS's caveat on "A" is
-- carried into the answer text: an A indicator means payable under the
-- fee schedule, NOT a national coverage determination — the A/B MAC
-- remains responsible for coverage where no national policy exists.
--
-- WHY THIS MATTERS BEYOND COVERAGE: 99417 carries status I — "not valid
-- for Medicare purposes, Medicare uses another code". Billing 99417 to
-- Medicare is a denial; G0318 (status A, $34.07) is the code Medicare
-- wants for prolonged home or residence services. That rule alone
-- prevents a recurring denial.
--
-- 99343 does not appear on the fee schedule at all. Taken with Ohio
-- Medicaid listing it as discontinued from 01/01/2023, that is two
-- independent confirmations the code is retired — which is why the NC
-- schedule's stale listing of it was withheld from the state seed.
--
-- Medicare is federal; payer_rule.state is NOT NULL, so each rule is
-- written once per state the practice operates in (OH/NC/SC).
--
-- 48 rules (16 codes x 3 states).
-- Idempotent: deterministic UUIDs + ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE.
--
-- DEPENDS ON db/seed/payer-medicare.sql having been applied — it defines
-- the Traditional Medicare (Part B) payer row this seed references. The
-- guard below fails loudly rather than leaving a confusing FK error.

BEGIN;

DO $$
BEGIN
  IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM payer WHERE id = 'a0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000401'::uuid) THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'Traditional Medicare (Part B) payer row is missing. Apply db/seed/payer-medicare.sql first.';
  END IF;
END $$;

